00:44:25.518 --> 00:44:30.158
So after we had, um, met with
the stakeholders, right, my

00:44:30.178 --> 00:44:32.538
boss, um, gave us a task.

00:44:33.058 --> 00:44:38.589
So in, in our, in our, my place
of work, that's Ecobank, and we

00:44:38.589 --> 00:44:44.153
do have this community on Teams,
right, where everybody on board from

00:44:44.250 --> 00:44:49.286
around, um, the various branches in
the different countries, right, we

00:44:49.287 --> 00:44:50.725
are all on that community, right?

00:44:50.741 --> 00:44:57.653
So my boss tasked us to be posting
about UX, about accessibility, and of

00:44:57.667 --> 00:45:03.386
course I was sharing videos, um, on
Be My Eyes, how Be My Eyes is doing.

00:45:03.749 --> 00:45:07.384
I was sharing videos or articles
on digital accessibility.

00:45:07.953 --> 00:45:12.370
And we had people like viewing
this and post, commenting about it.

00:45:12.906 --> 00:45:16.131
And then before we knew it, it
was like a mandatory course,

00:45:16.801 --> 00:45:18.450
like for everyone to be on board.

00:45:18.490 --> 00:45:26.548
And then also for, um, for the
developers and then for the, the

00:45:26.605 --> 00:45:31.270
technical guys in our, um, in our,
my place of work, that's Ecobank.

00:45:32.694 --> 00:45:39.577
So my boss made me understand that
or through my research I, I got

00:45:39.586 --> 00:45:44.662
to found, I found out that, um,
when… You can't do, you can't do

00:45:44.667 --> 00:45:46.548
the business field alone, right?

00:45:46.712 --> 00:45:48.587
You need to have everybody else on board.

00:45:48.924 --> 00:45:53.495
Because as a designer, I would design the
website, I would design the mobile app,

00:45:54.357 --> 00:45:56.278
but then I hand off to the developer.

00:45:56.980 --> 00:46:00.356
So if the developer has no idea
about accessibility or digital

00:46:00.997 --> 00:46:03.953
accessibility, he's just gonna go
about his normal day of like coding

00:46:03.961 --> 00:46:06.337
and not even thinking about it, right?

00:46:06.841 --> 00:46:11.778
And then he's just gonna publish, uh, what
he has to publish, and then they move on.

00:46:12.221 --> 00:46:16.638
But then when you bring these people
on board, you get them to understand

00:46:16.680 --> 00:46:21.810
little by little, and then they get to
appreciate it, and then they include it.

00:46:22.116 --> 00:46:28.232
So I remember there was this time, um,
I went to see one of, um, my bosses, um,

00:46:28.540 --> 00:46:34.839
about, um, the way forward with digital
accessibility when it comes to Ecobank.

00:46:34.881 --> 00:46:40.162
And then he was like, "Oh, um, for 2026,
um, we've already like had conversations

00:46:40.162 --> 00:46:45.096
with the dev- the developers to include,
uh, digital accessibility in their code.

00:46:45.470 --> 00:46:50.529
So we can seem to make that, yeah, it's
making a difference in their code, right?

00:46:50.529 --> 00:46:56.042
But then for 2027, um, we're gonna make
sure that, uh, a proper draft or a proper

00:46:56.091 --> 00:46:58.741
budget draft, um, for digital access-

00:47:01.316 --> 00:47:01.875
Gary: Excellent.

00:47:01.897 --> 00:47:02.216
Yeah.

00:47:02.229 --> 00:47:07.221
So, um, yeah, it's a good point that, uh,
developers need to be on board as well,

00:47:07.258 --> 00:47:11.391
um, because they've already got so many
other things to think about, so they're

00:47:11.395 --> 00:47:15.229
like, "Oh, yeah." This is another thing
that you need that buy-in, don't you?

00:47:15.854 --> 00:47:17.444
Um, excellent.

